WEBVTT

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:16.660
<i>Along a zigzag the world turns,</i>
<i>I heave out a sigh.</i>

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:27.670
<i>Someone pauses along the way,</i>
<i>but reality moves on.</i>

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:33.200
<i>Treat love as love, treat</i>
<i>dreams as dreams.</i>

00:00:33.310 --> 00:00:38.710
<i>It's difficult to say it in earnest.</i>
<i>The times forge ahead, but...</i>

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:43.620
<i>I want to make you happy...</i>

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:49.420
<i>I'll do so like I do to</i>
<i>be myself. Yeah!</i><i>I'll do so like I do to</i>
<i>be myself. Yeah!</i>

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:54.450
<i>I'll make you happy...</i>

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:59.870
<i>I dedicate all that</i>
<i>I can do to you.</i>

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:11.180
<i>Along a zigzag the world turns,</i>
<i>I heave out a sigh.</i>

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:23.430
<i>Someone pauses along the way,</i>
<i>but love doesn't stop for me.</i>

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:49.410
Let's see...

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:55.220
All right!

00:01:56.590 --> 00:01:57.690
Yippee...

00:02:12.380 --> 00:02:13.970
Wow!

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:19.200
FILE. 11
SANTA CLAUS PANIC

00:02:23.150 --> 00:02:26.850
Santa, make my wish
come true this year.

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:34.220
Santa only brings presents to good
girls and boys, you know?

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:36.700
Then I'm in! 'Cause
I'm a good girl!

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:38.460
Oh, I wonder!

00:02:38.570 --> 00:02:42.470
Didn't you have to make a report yesterday
about having broken some equipment?

00:02:43.570 --> 00:02:46.630
That was so long ago, I've
forgotten about that.

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:49.070
Oh! I think you dropped
a stitch there.

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:53.080
Oh, you're right! And I'm
running out of time.

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:56.450
Miyuki, is that a Xmas
present for someone?

00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:59.710
Nakajima will love
it, I'm sure.

00:02:59.890 --> 00:03:03.350
W... Who said I was giving
it to Nakajima?

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:07.060
Who else wears
a size this big?

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:15.430
Beg your pardon?
Yes, right.

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:17.940
Dinner for two at 6;00
on Christmas Eve.

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:21.480
Yes, two special
dinner courses.

00:03:21.580 --> 00:03:23.440
That's right. Two.
Thank you.

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:27.610
All righty!

00:03:29.990 --> 00:03:35.080
This Xmas Eve for sure... just
me and Kobayakawa...

00:03:50.670 --> 00:03:54.610
What? What are you looking
at? Something happening?

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:57.270
Cheers!

00:03:57.380 --> 00:04:00.010
You look absolutely
radiant, darling.

00:04:01.350 --> 00:04:03.980
Gee, you're
so honest!

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:05.350
Kobayakawa!

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:07.490
Nakajima!

00:04:09.790 --> 00:04:12.590
I'm sure that's what Nakajima
is thinking, too.

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:16.720
That's silly. I don't have a date
with him on Christmas Eve.

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:22.270
Nakajima can be pretty shy. I'm sure he's
just waiting for the chance to invite you.

00:04:22.370 --> 00:04:27.540
That's right. I saw him pouring over
fancy restaurant magazines.

00:04:29.780 --> 00:04:33.220
Would you cut it out! Hey,
Natsumi, it's patrol time!

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:35.180
Be right with
you.

00:04:35.350 --> 00:04:38.190
Oh, yeah. Could you take the
tree to the lobby, Natsumi?

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:40.790
Sure will, no
problem.

00:04:40.890 --> 00:04:42.980
Yippee!

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:55.960
By the way, what did you wish
for from Santa Claus?

00:04:56.870 --> 00:04:57.770
Wanna know?

00:04:57.940 --> 00:04:59.240
Not if you don't
want to tell.

00:04:59.410 --> 00:05:02.110
Well I do, and I want
you to listen!

00:05:02.210 --> 00:05:05.340
This year I'm spending Christmas
Eve with the Chief.

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:06.970
A romantic night
together.

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:15.190
<i>"I love you."</i>

00:05:18.230 --> 00:05:20.420
Oh? But he's working
on Christmas Eve.

00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:22.160
Huh?

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:29.130
Look, there are some good little kids who'll
be getting presents from Santa this year.

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:34.480
I really, really want that!

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:35.150
I really want this!

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:37.580
This is the present I want!

00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:39.310
That's the one
I want to get!

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:43.250
Hey. Bad kids who loiter around
won't be getting...

00:05:43.350 --> 00:05:45.820
...any presents
from Santa.

00:05:46.590 --> 00:05:47.820
Hey, it's
Miyuki!

00:05:47.990 --> 00:05:50.320
I'm not counting
on Santa...

00:05:50.430 --> 00:05:52.050
...my Dad's gonna
get it for me!

00:05:52.230 --> 00:05:53.860
What happened to the
Christmas spirit?

00:05:54.030 --> 00:05:56.690
Or Natsumi could get it for me!
Will you buy that for me?

00:06:00.140 --> 00:06:02.100
Maho?

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:04.030
What's the
matter?

00:06:04.210 --> 00:06:07.510
Is Santa Claus
a bad man?

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:11.140
She said she
saw Santa.

00:06:11.310 --> 00:06:14.180
But he did bad
things.

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:16.340
What do you
mean?

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:18.780
At my house
last night...

00:06:21.630 --> 00:06:23.290
<i>"Oh, Santa!"</i>

00:06:24.590 --> 00:06:27.430
<i>"Keep quiet. Or you'll wake up</i>
<i>your mommy and daddy."</i>

00:06:27.530 --> 00:06:30.500
<i>"Uh... grown-ups aren't</i>
<i>supposed to see me."</i>

00:06:32.970 --> 00:06:36.460
<i>"Wow! You really</i>
<i>are Santa!"</i>

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:39.610
<i>"I sure am. I just</i>
<i>came to..."</i>

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:41.770
<i>"...check and see if you've been</i>
<i>a good girl this year."</i>

00:06:41.950 --> 00:06:44.040
<i>"Yup! I've been a
good girl!"</i>

00:06:44.850 --> 00:06:48.980
<i>"I'm sure! There'll be a present for</i>
<i>you under the tree this year."</i>

00:06:49.290 --> 00:06:54.250
<i>"So... don't tell your mommy or daddy</i>
<i>that you saw me here tonight. Okay?"</i>

00:06:54.590 --> 00:06:56.080
<i>"OK. I won't tell</i>
<i>anybody."</i>

00:06:56.260 --> 00:06:58.230
<i>"You're a good</i>
<i>little girl."</i>

00:06:59.830 --> 00:07:01.690
<i>"What a haul."</i>

00:07:02.570 --> 00:07:04.530
<i>"Come again,</i>
<i>Santa."</i>

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:25.380
Santa took mommy's jewelry
and her money.

00:07:29.330 --> 00:07:31.660
That was a thief!
He's a bad man!

00:07:31.830 --> 00:07:33.820
Is Santa a
bad man?

00:07:33.960 --> 00:07:35.530
No, not at all, Maho.

00:07:35.530 --> 00:07:36.970
He was just a fake Santa.

00:07:37.130 --> 00:07:38.190
Natsumi!

00:07:38.370 --> 00:07:41.700
The real Santa loves good kids and
would never do something like that.

00:07:41.970 --> 00:07:43.460
Really?

00:07:43.640 --> 00:07:46.770
Yes! You have to believe
in the real Santa.

00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:49.900
We're gonna catch
that fake Santa.

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:53.410
How dare that phony trample on the
dreams of innocent children.

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:56.920
I won't stand for it, whatever
anyone else says!

00:07:57.020 --> 00:07:58.920
I'm gonna catch
him!

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:02.310
Look at Natsumi!
Neat-o!

00:08:02.490 --> 00:08:03.960
Thank you. Thank
you very much.

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:07.430
"Investigation Section"

00:08:07.430 --> 00:08:11.830
Yeah, that's right. There've been a
number of robberies in this area.

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:14.060
Any leads yet?

00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:16.210
Not especially.

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:21.070
But there've been sightings of a strange
man dressed as Santa Claus lately.

00:08:22.780 --> 00:08:26.080
What is it? You know
something?

00:08:26.250 --> 00:08:27.650
Not yet.

00:08:27.820 --> 00:08:30.840
You're in the wrong section.
You two are with traffic.

00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:35.680
But we really want to catch
this guy ourselves.

00:08:41.260 --> 00:08:45.220
All right, I see. I don't think I can
stop you just by telling you to.

00:08:46.300 --> 00:08:48.360
Thank you for
the materials.

00:08:48.510 --> 00:08:49.970
Thanks.

00:08:52.710 --> 00:08:55.940
By the way, Mr. Tokuno, what do you
have planned for Christmas Eve?

00:08:56.450 --> 00:08:58.970
I'm working. The year-end can be
pretty perilous with crime and all.

00:08:59.080 --> 00:09:00.710
No time for
a break!

00:09:00.880 --> 00:09:02.650
Oh, yeah. I
guess so.

00:09:10.260 --> 00:09:11.990
Oh! Hey, Kobayakawa!

00:09:12.560 --> 00:09:15.000
Good timing! I've some-
thing to ask you.

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:16.730
Sorry Nakajima.

00:09:16.830 --> 00:09:17.960
We're in a big rush.
It'll have to wait.

00:09:21.470 --> 00:09:23.300
He sure cleaned
them out!

00:09:23.410 --> 00:09:26.930
Jewelry, cash, antiques,
a lamp, underwear...

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:29.270
...and even the contents
of the fridge.

00:09:29.450 --> 00:09:34.140
And a number of other houses were
broken into on the same day.

00:09:34.250 --> 00:09:37.690
How would he carry away all these things
without looking conspicuous?

00:09:38.250 --> 00:09:42.090
Yeah, how would he carry a big
bag without raising suspicion?

00:09:43.260 --> 00:09:44.750
Aha! That's why he's
disguised as Santa.

00:09:44.930 --> 00:09:48.420
Right. Who would think
twice about Santa...

00:09:48.530 --> 00:09:50.120
...carrying
a big bag?

00:09:50.300 --> 00:09:54.260
That's totally despicable! Using Santa's
image for such an evil deed!

00:09:54.440 --> 00:09:55.670
You sure are taking
this personally!

00:09:55.840 --> 00:09:57.670
Damn right, girl!

00:09:57.770 --> 00:10:02.210
When I was a kid, I wanted to see
what the real Santa looked like.

00:10:02.310 --> 00:10:07.220
So in grammar school I pretended to be
asleep and found out it was my Dad.

00:10:07.320 --> 00:10:09.950
What a shock
that was.

00:10:10.120 --> 00:10:14.680
So we really have to make sure that
Maho's dreams aren't shattered.

00:10:14.860 --> 00:10:17.380
I won't forgive you,
you phony Santa!

00:10:17.560 --> 00:10:20.190
Natsumi! Miyuki! There's been
a sighting of a weird Santa!

00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:22.190
Where?!

00:10:30.410 --> 00:10:33.860
"This man has littered, so I have given
him this garbage as a present."

00:10:34.010 --> 00:10:36.140
"Signed, Santa
Claus Man."

00:10:36.410 --> 00:10:39.850
I know someone who would
do something like this.

00:10:40.020 --> 00:10:41.950
That makes
two of us.

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:45.210
Over there!

00:10:45.890 --> 00:10:48.220
I was just giving someone
directions...

00:10:48.320 --> 00:10:51.260
...and this big man came up to
me and called me a hooker.

00:10:51.760 --> 00:10:53.960
It was so scary!

00:10:57.800 --> 00:10:59.770
Wha?! It's that
Santa Claus!

00:11:15.890 --> 00:11:17.410
Let's go, Black
Dragon!

00:11:17.590 --> 00:11:19.850
Stop right
there!

00:11:20.020 --> 00:11:21.920
You're the Strike
Man!

00:11:22.430 --> 00:11:25.390
"Strike Man?!" Never
heard of him.

00:11:27.130 --> 00:11:29.100
I'm the Defender
of Justice!

00:11:30.600 --> 00:11:32.260
The Santa Claus
Man!

00:11:32.440 --> 00:11:34.840
Oh yeah? Then what's that
"S" for on your mask?

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:37.530
"S" for Santa,
what else?

00:11:37.710 --> 00:11:39.800
I see you've painted your
motorbike bright red.

00:11:40.210 --> 00:11:42.070
You fool!

00:11:42.180 --> 00:11:46.210
How dare you call this a mere motorbike!
I'll have you know that his name is...

00:11:46.350 --> 00:11:49.440
...Black Dragon Richard Mason
Harold De Dion Plimms...

00:11:49.550 --> 00:11:51.540
...Stuart Kazuaki
the 3rd!

00:11:51.720 --> 00:11:53.280
Dare you to try repeating
that one!

00:11:53.460 --> 00:11:56.430
Hmph! Black Dragon Richard
Ma... Menthol Ha... Halogen...

00:11:57.630 --> 00:12:01.530
...Pudding ala Mode...
the 3rd!

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:04.100
Not exactly the same
as before...

00:12:04.270 --> 00:12:06.260
It matters not!

00:12:06.700 --> 00:12:11.040
Oh, your powerful body! Ooh, baby,
you're looking good today...

00:12:11.210 --> 00:12:12.570
You share the same
interests.

00:12:12.740 --> 00:12:15.910
Leave me alone. I'm not a
machine freak, like he is.

00:12:16.080 --> 00:12:21.020
My Black Dragon and I have a mission;
to deliver happiness to the world!

00:12:21.180 --> 00:12:24.550
Quit making yourself out to be such a
hero. And what's with the get-up?

00:12:24.650 --> 00:12:27.150
Think you can pass
for Santa Claus?

00:12:27.260 --> 00:12:29.120
Wait a minute...

00:12:29.230 --> 00:12:31.590
Were you the one who broke into
Maho's house the other night?

00:12:31.760 --> 00:12:34.230
I don't have a clue what
you're talking about.

00:12:34.400 --> 00:12:38.160
I know you've been up to a lot of
weird things, but I had no idea!

00:12:38.330 --> 00:12:40.030
So what are you
talking about?

00:12:40.200 --> 00:12:44.160
Gonna play dumb with me? Confess
to your misdeeds, my man!

00:12:44.340 --> 00:12:45.810
Come on,
Natsumi.

00:12:45.980 --> 00:12:46.500
Whatcha want!

00:12:46.680 --> 00:12:52.110
I can't imagine little Maho mistaking
this weirdo for the real Santa!

00:12:52.280 --> 00:12:55.010
You're right about that! He's a weirdo,
no matter how you look at him.

00:12:55.180 --> 00:12:58.590
Insolence! I am
the real Santa!

00:12:59.060 --> 00:13:01.110
Oh, no! I don't have time for
this. I must be going!

00:13:01.290 --> 00:13:02.310
Hey, wait!

00:13:02.490 --> 00:13:06.450
I must hurry and deliver presents to
the good little boys and girls!

00:13:07.800 --> 00:13:09.560
Miyuki, we've got
to follow him!

00:13:09.730 --> 00:13:13.860
He's not the robber we're after, but
we can't just let him go like that!

00:13:14.400 --> 00:13:17.970
Tsujimoto! Kobayakawa! Where are
you? That robber has struck again!

00:13:21.180 --> 00:13:23.610
According to a lady in
the neighborhood...

00:13:23.710 --> 00:13:26.440
...the alleged Santa was lurking
around here a few hours ago.

00:13:26.620 --> 00:13:28.780
First the Strike Man,
and now this thief!

00:13:28.890 --> 00:13:32.750
What's going on with all
these weird Santas?!

00:13:37.330 --> 00:13:39.420
What happened
to her?

00:13:39.860 --> 00:13:42.920
This great big guy who called
himself Santa Claus Man...

00:13:43.770 --> 00:13:47.260
...decided to give her
a kiss for a present!

00:13:47.440 --> 00:13:49.670
Stop it! It's grossing
me out!

00:13:49.840 --> 00:13:51.970
That Strike Man! He won't
get away with it!

00:13:52.140 --> 00:13:55.410
The Santa Claus Man
is the Strike Man?

00:13:55.510 --> 00:13:58.450
In that case, he's right
behind you!

00:14:01.850 --> 00:14:05.340
Why didn't you
tell us sooner!

00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:19.700
You see how he turned
that corner?!

00:14:19.800 --> 00:14:21.770
With his muffler scraping
on the road!

00:14:24.770 --> 00:14:27.300
It's no use! We can't
keep up with him!

00:14:36.590 --> 00:14:38.880
We've completely
lost him.

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:44.080
Santa Claus is someone who lives
in your dreams. He's like a saint.

00:14:44.190 --> 00:14:46.090
This is terrible!

00:14:47.400 --> 00:14:49.300
Miyuki! Look!

00:14:49.470 --> 00:14:51.490
A thief!

00:14:51.670 --> 00:14:54.640
I've got you now,
you impostor!

00:15:01.580 --> 00:15:02.940
Stop!

00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:07.720
We're not going
to let you go!

00:15:16.660 --> 00:15:17.160
"Christmas Sale... - Dec. 10 to Dec. 25"

00:15:17.160 --> 00:15:18.790
What on earth
is this?

00:15:19.660 --> 00:15:22.890
How are we gonna find
our thief now?

00:15:23.700 --> 00:15:26.670
What's with all these
Santas?!

00:15:26.900 --> 00:15:28.630
Well, it is Christmas
after all.

00:15:30.610 --> 00:15:32.100
In other words...

00:15:32.210 --> 00:15:37.170
...our thief dressed up as Santa
so that he'd blend in.

00:15:37.350 --> 00:15:40.870
Exactly. Because
of Strike Man...

00:15:40.980 --> 00:15:43.380
...I can't make heads or tails of all
these weird Santa sightings.

00:15:45.720 --> 00:15:49.250
We'll have to do something about him, or
he'll shatter the dreams of our children.

00:15:49.430 --> 00:15:53.120
That's true, but also, we only have a certain
amount of time to find our thief.

00:15:53.300 --> 00:15:53.920
What?

00:15:54.100 --> 00:15:58.090
Our thief can only dress up as
Santa until Christmas Eve.

00:15:58.200 --> 00:16:01.400
After that he'll stick out
like a sore thumb.

00:16:01.570 --> 00:16:03.510
So what do we do? Tomorrow's
Christmas Eve.

00:16:03.670 --> 00:16:06.230
We'll have to analyze
his movements...

00:16:06.340 --> 00:16:09.310
...based on the places where
he's committed robberies.

00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:16.250
Tomorrow's Christmas Eve, and
I still haven't asked her...

00:16:16.890 --> 00:16:20.250
The thief seems to be most active
in this residential area.

00:16:21.860 --> 00:16:25.320
There are lots of shops around here, so
it'd be easy for him to make a getaway.

00:16:25.800 --> 00:16:29.230
All we can do is wait for
him to strike again.

00:16:30.900 --> 00:16:34.600
Nothing unusual here. The robber
and the Santa Claus Man...

00:16:34.700 --> 00:16:37.230
...rather, the Strike Man, are
nowhere to be found.

00:16:38.510 --> 00:16:40.000
Nothing to report
here, either.

00:16:40.180 --> 00:16:43.240
Roger. Nakajima, could you
proceed to the next area?

00:16:43.410 --> 00:16:46.580
Roger... By the way,
Kobayakawa?

00:16:46.750 --> 00:16:48.180
What's that? Want
to talk to Miyuki?

00:16:48.350 --> 00:16:51.810
Uh, Tsujimoto.
Uh, nothing.

00:16:51.990 --> 00:16:53.720
Sure?

00:16:54.290 --> 00:16:57.230
<i>What a loser</i>
<i>I am.</i>

00:16:57.790 --> 00:17:00.230
Weirdo.

00:17:00.330 --> 00:17:04.230
How can he be so elusive when
we're all searching like this?

00:17:04.630 --> 00:17:09.700
That's how it goes. We can rush,
but it's not gonna help much.

00:17:16.180 --> 00:17:23.280
It's been a job well-done.
Just a little more to go.

00:17:31.490 --> 00:17:32.520
What was
that?

00:17:32.700 --> 00:17:34.390
Over there!

00:17:34.560 --> 00:17:37.460
How dare you throw away
your cigarette like that?!

00:17:37.570 --> 00:17:41.470
As a fellow Santa Claus, I cannot
let you get away with this!

00:17:42.440 --> 00:17:44.130
So we meet again,
Strike Man.

00:17:44.310 --> 00:17:48.040
Why you... I'm telling you,
I'm Santa Claus Man!

00:17:50.110 --> 00:17:51.810
Look, there's a pig
flying up there!

00:17:51.980 --> 00:17:53.780
What? Where?

00:17:53.950 --> 00:17:54.880
Hah!

00:17:55.050 --> 00:17:57.450
Aah!

00:17:57.620 --> 00:17:59.280
Got it!

00:17:59.390 --> 00:18:01.880
Now we'll find out
your true identity!

00:18:01.990 --> 00:18:04.960
And you'll never get away
with your mischief!

00:18:05.130 --> 00:18:12.330
Oh, no! You've discovered
that I'm the Strike Man!

00:18:12.500 --> 00:18:14.800
I see you've got another
mask on.

00:18:14.970 --> 00:18:19.340
Now I have no other choice! I'll see
you again, Home Run Girl!

00:18:19.510 --> 00:18:21.410
I told you I don't appreciate
that name!

00:18:21.580 --> 00:18:23.440
There's no point
fighting it.

00:18:24.750 --> 00:18:29.710
Anyway, we won't be hearing
from him for awhile.

00:18:34.920 --> 00:18:36.890
Oh, I see you've
woken up.

00:18:37.860 --> 00:18:39.420
<i>The police!</i>

00:18:39.930 --> 00:18:41.690
Are you alright, sir?

00:18:42.160 --> 00:18:45.600
Uh, yeah, well I have
work to do...

00:18:45.700 --> 00:18:46.370
...so I'd better be going...

00:18:46.370 --> 00:18:50.170
Oh, you forgot something! Here.

00:18:51.110 --> 00:18:52.600
Oh, no!

00:18:52.780 --> 00:18:55.770
Huh? Oh,
my!

00:18:55.880 --> 00:18:57.870
What do we
have here?

00:18:58.050 --> 00:19:01.640
Stop, you phony
Santa Claus!

00:19:03.750 --> 00:19:06.310
I was wrong!

00:19:08.190 --> 00:19:11.390
Looks like this time we should
be grateful to the Strike Man.

00:19:12.330 --> 00:19:15.130
Who would have thought that
he'd save the day, huh?!

00:19:42.160 --> 00:19:45.650
Santa? The
real one?

00:19:45.830 --> 00:19:49.260
That's right. I'm the
real Santa Claus.

00:19:49.930 --> 00:19:50.830
Really?

00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:55.130
Yes! That bad Santa
Claus was caught.

00:19:55.240 --> 00:19:59.370
And, since you've been such a good
girl, I'm giving you this present.

00:19:59.540 --> 00:20:01.510
Wow!

00:20:03.050 --> 00:20:04.570
Thank you!

00:20:04.750 --> 00:20:08.580
Bye-bye. Always be a
good little girl!

00:20:08.750 --> 00:20:10.720
I will.

00:20:15.420 --> 00:20:19.020
Wow! Thank
you, Santa!

00:20:22.060 --> 00:20:24.590
That was nice
of you.

00:20:24.770 --> 00:20:26.560
It was nothing.

00:20:26.740 --> 00:20:30.760
Pretty smooth, dressing up as Santa to
make a little girl's dreams come true.

00:20:30.940 --> 00:20:34.380
Yes. Thanks for helping
us out, Nakajima.

00:20:34.540 --> 00:20:36.510
Don't mention it.

00:20:38.810 --> 00:20:44.120
Oh, no! Look at the time! I missed
my reservation at that restaurant!

00:20:44.220 --> 00:20:48.180
My special dinner
course...

00:20:53.100 --> 00:20:55.060
Looks like a
perfect fit.

00:20:56.330 --> 00:21:00.360
I just finished knitting
it for you.

00:21:00.470 --> 00:21:02.030
Here you
are.

00:21:02.200 --> 00:21:04.170
What? For me?

00:21:06.440 --> 00:21:10.780
Thanks a lot, Kobayakawa.

00:21:15.580 --> 00:21:18.550
I'll take good
care of it.

00:21:22.390 --> 00:21:24.760
Oh, dear Santa
Claus...

00:21:24.860 --> 00:21:28.130
Please bring me
happiness!

00:21:33.700 --> 00:21:35.970
Yippee! It snowed!

00:21:35.970 --> 00:21:36.110
Let's make another snowman!

00:21:36.110 --> 00:21:37.570
Yippee!

00:22:04.830 --> 00:22:06.840
<i>I live my life my own way, doing</i>
<i>things others wouldn't.</i>

00:22:11.170 --> 00:22:19.010
<i>Being strong isn't enough.</i>
<i>It makes me Ionely.</i>

00:22:21.720 --> 00:22:30.030
<i>I can feel your presence</i>
<i>as if you're right here...</i>

00:22:30.560 --> 00:22:38.130
<i>... but I can't say a word.</i>

00:22:39.600 --> 00:22:46.870
<i>The feelings I hide within might</i>
<i>break into pieces...</i>

00:22:48.410 --> 00:22:55.780
<i>But if I don't say anything,</i>
<i>nothing can begin.</i>

00:22:56.120 --> 00:23:03.350
<i>The wind gently blows...</i>
<i>Time flows...</i>

00:23:03.530 --> 00:23:13.070
<i>Time flows... And soon</i>
<i>I can be honest...</i>

00:23:13.200 --> 00:23:16.130
<i>Thank you,</i>
<i>friend!</i>

00:23:22.310 --> 00:23:24.340
"High School Girls"

00:23:24.950 --> 00:23:26.850
Cellphone and Oshou... Cell and Oshou...

00:23:26.850 --> 00:23:28.010
Whatcha mumbling about?

00:23:28.180 --> 00:23:30.450
The clues we have are;
Cell, Oshou, and milk!

00:23:30.450 --> 00:23:31.980
No! You can't possibly use your head!

00:23:32.150 --> 00:23:34.820
Nakajima says that's one thing he
doesn't want to hear from you.

00:23:34.990 --> 00:23:38.120
Gotta do something quick, or
our high school friend will be...

00:23:38.290 --> 00:23:41.490
A high school student? Then, we got Cell,
Oshou, milk and high school student...

00:23:41.600 --> 00:23:43.260
Hmm, things are getting
more confusing!

00:23:43.430 --> 00:23:45.470
Next time on You're Under Arrest, File 12,
"I Want To Be A Policewoman!"

00:23:45.470 --> 00:23:46.840
FILE. 12
I WANT TO BE A
POLICEWOMAN!

00:23:46.840 --> 00:23:48.840
Cell, Oshou, milk... and
high school girls...
